  "cards": [
    {
      "title": "Two Different Caches",
      "dot": "cyan",
      "items": [
        "MLA stores a 512-wide latent per original token. KPool compresses only 128-wide retrieval keys; main attention does not read pooled V.",
        "The indexer derives queries from Q latent and keys/compression gates/head weights from hidden. It uses 32 retrieval heads versus 64 main attention heads.",
        "2048 is the main historical token budget: select at most 512 full groups, expand each to 4 original tokens, then include 0–3 visible tail tokens."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Dependencies, Not a Fixed Schedule",
      "dot": "amber",
      "items": [
        "This depicts a layer that runs its indexer. Short-sequence shortcuts, top-k reuse, FP8 packing, and projection fusion may change physical execution.",
        "NoPE removes text MLA RoPE; causal positions, request boundaries, and page tables remain necessary."
      ]
    }
  ]
